(95, 3, 4, 64, '<p>Mohan starts from point A and walks 1Km towards south, turns left and walks 1 km. Then he turns left again and walks 1km. Now he is facing</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 786, 0, 0, NULL),
(98, 3, 4, 65, '<p>John divided his property among his three sons- Tom, Dick and Harry. Harry&rsquo;s son Mathew had some dispute with Dick&rsquo;s son. Mathew&rsquo;s son Ivan helped in solving the dispute later. State the relation between Ivan and John.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 797, 0, 0, NULL),
(99, 3, 5, 66, '<p>What is V&rsquo;s profession?</p>\r\n', '<p>P, Q, R, S, T, V and W are travelling in three different vehicles. There are at least two passengers in each vehicle I, II &amp; III and only one of them is a male. There are two engineers, two doctors and three teachers among them.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>i) R is a lady doctor and she does not travel with the pair of sisters P and V.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>ii) Q, a male engineer, travels only with W a teacher in vehicle I.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iii) S is a male doctor</p>\r\n\r\n<p>iv) Two person belonging to the same profession do not travel in the same vehicle.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>v) P is not an engineer and travels in vehicle II.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 800, 0, 0, NULL),
(100, 3, 5, 66, '<p>In which vehicle R does travel?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 805, 0, 0, NULL),
(101, 3, 5, 66, '<p>Which of the following represents the teacher?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 808, 0, 0, NULL),
(102, 3, 5, 66, '<p>Which of the following is not correct?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 814, 0, 0, NULL),
(103, 3, 5, 66, '<p>How many lady members are there?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 817, 0, 0, NULL),
(104, 3, 5, 66, '<p>what is T&rsquo;s profession?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 819, 0, 0, NULL),
(106, 3, 4, 67, '<p><em><strong>Statements</strong>:</em></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(i) All fans are rooms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) No room is green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(iii) Some windows are green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Conclusions:</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(I) Some windows are fan.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(II) Some windows are rooms.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(III) Some fans are green.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(IV) No green is fan.</p>\r\n', '<p>In each of the questions below are given few statements followed by few conclusions numbered. Considering the given statements to be true, read all conclusions and then decide which of the given conclusion logically follow the given statement.</p>\r\n', 'No', 1, 829, 0, 0, NULL),
(107, 3, 4, 67, '<p><strong><em>Statements:</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(i) Some books are pen.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(ii) No pen is pencil.</p>\r\n\r\n<p><strong><em>Conclusions:</em></strong></p>\r\n\r\n<p>(I) Some books are pencil.</p>\r\n\r\n<p>(II) No book is pencil.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 832, 0, 0, NULL),
(108, 3, 2, 68, '<p>Rajinish is older than Rajesh and Raman. Ramesh is older than Rajesh but youger than Rajeev. Raman is older than Rajeev. Who among them is oldest.</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 837, 0, 0, NULL),
(109, 3, 5, 69, '<p>A, B and C are sisters. D is the brother of E and E is the daughter of B. How is A related to D?</p>\r\n', '', 'No', 1, 842, 0, 0, NULL),
